[{"id":"starter","dot":"👋","name":"Starter","title":"Starter Unit","sub":"Saludos, instrucciones y útiles","rules":"\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>1. Los saludos se aprenden de a pares</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">What's your name?</span><span class=\"ra\">My name's Ana.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">How are you?</span><span class=\"ra\">I'm fine, thanks!</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">How old are you?</span><span class=\"ra\">I'm six years old.</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">No hay regla que estudiar: es pregunta &rarr; respuesta. Se memorizan juntas.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>2. Las contracciones (el ap&oacute;strofe)</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">What's</span><span class=\"ra\">= What is</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">My name's</span><span class=\"ra\">= My name is</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">I'm</span><span class=\"ra\">= I am</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">El ap&oacute;strofe reemplaza una letra que se borr&oacute;. Siempre significa lo mismo.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>3. Las instrucciones de clase son &oacute;rdenes</h4>\n<p class=\"exline\">El verbo va primero y solo: <b>Stand</b> up. <b>Open</b> your books. <b>Sit</b> down. No llevan sujeto adelante.</p></div>\n","ex":[{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada pregunta con su respuesta","pairs":[["What's your name?","My name's Ana."],["How are you?","I'm fine, thanks!"],["Hello!","Hi!"],["Good morning!","Good morning, Miss!"]]},{"t":"choice","q":"La maestra dice: <span class='en'>Stand up</span>","h":"¿Qué tenés que hacer?","o":["Pararme","Sentarme","Abrir el libro"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Open your books</span> significa:","o":["Abran los libros","Cierren los libros","Guarden los lápices"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Put away your pencils</span> significa:","o":["Saquen los lápices","Guarden los lápices","Presten los lápices"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Sit down, please.</span>","o":["Sentate, por favor","Parate, por favor","Cerrá el libro"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","e":"✏️","q":"<span class='en'>What is it?</span>","o":["It's a pencil.","It's a pen.","It's a rubber."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","e":"🎒","q":"<span class='en'>What is it?</span>","o":["It's a ruler.","It's a schoolbag.","It's a book."],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice <b>lapicera</b>?","o":["pencil","crayon","pen"],"a":2},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>goma</b>","a":"rubber"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>regla</b>","a":"ruler"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>cartuchera</b>","a":"pencil case"},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Take out your pencils</span> significa:","o":["Guarden los lápices","Saquen los lápices","Presten los lápices"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Close your books</span> significa:","o":["Cierren los libros","Abran los libros","Lean los libros"],"a":0}]},{"id":"u1","dot":"🎂","name":"Unit 1","title":"Unit 1","sub":"How old are you? · he/she · colores y números","rules":"\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>1. El verbo TO BE (ser / estar / tener a&ntilde;os)</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">I</span><span class=\"ra\">am</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">he / she / it</span><span class=\"ra\">is</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">you / we / they</span><span class=\"ra\">are</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">En ingl&eacute;s la edad se dice con <b>to be</b>, no con \"tener\": <b>I am</b> six years old (literal: \"yo soy seis\").</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>2. Para preguntar, se da vuelta</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">You are seven.</span><span class=\"ra\">Are you seven?</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">She is six.</span><span class=\"ra\">Is she six?</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">El verbo salta al principio. Nada m&aacute;s cambia.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>3. Respuestas cortas</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Are you seven?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, I am. / No, I'm not.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Is she six?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, she is. / No, she isn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>&#9888; Error t&iacute;pico:</b> en el <span class=\"yes\">S&Iacute;</span> nunca se contrae. Se dice <span class=\"yes\">Yes, I am</span>, nunca <span class=\"no\">Yes, I'm</span>. En el <b>NO</b> s&iacute;: No, I'm not.</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>4. HIS o HER: depende del DUE&Ntilde;O</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Tom &rarr; es var&oacute;n</span><span class=\"ra\">his name, his bag</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Ana &rarr; es mujer</span><span class=\"ra\">her name, her bag</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>&#9888; Ojo:</b> en castellano los dos son <b>\"su\"</b>, por eso se confunden. En ingl&eacute;s no mir&aacute;s la cosa, mir&aacute;s <b>de qui&eacute;n es</b>. La mochila de Tom es <b>his</b> bag aunque \"mochila\" sea femenino.</div></div>\n","ex":[{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>How old are you?</span>","h":"Tenés 6 años","o":["I'm six years old.","I'm fine, thanks.","My name's Tom."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Are you seven years old?</span>","h":"Respondé que SÍ","o":["Yes, I am.","Yes, I is.","Yes, I are."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Are you seven?</span>","h":"Respondé que NO","o":["No, I not.","No, I'm not.","No, I aren't."],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"This is Tom. ___ is seven.","o":["He","She","I"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"This is Mary. ___ isn't six.","o":["He","She","It"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>How old is she?</span>","h":"Ella tiene 6","o":["He's six.","She's six.","I'm six."],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"This is my friend Ben. ___ name is Ben.","o":["Her","His","Your"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"This is Ana. ___ favourite colour is red.","o":["His","Her","My"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>What colour is your schoolbag?</span>","h":"Es azul 🟦","o":["It's green.","It's blue.","It's black."],"a":1},{"t":"match","q":"Uní el color con su nombre","pairs":[["red","🔴 rojo"],["yellow","🟡 amarillo"],["brown","🟤 marrón"],["orange","🟠 naranja"],["green","🟢 verde"],["black","⚫ negro"],["white","⚪ blanco"],["blue","🔵 azul"]]},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí el número <b>7</b> en inglés","a":"seven"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí el número <b>4</b> en inglés","a":"four"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí el número <b>10</b> en inglés","a":"ten"},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada número con su palabra","pairs":[["one","1"],["two","2"],["three","3"],["five","5"],["six","6"],["eight","8"],["nine","9"]]},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>What's your favourite colour?</span>","h":"Tu color favorito es el blanco","o":["My favourite colour is white.","I'm white.","It's favourite white."],"a":0}]},{"id":"u2","dot":"👨‍👩‍👧","name":"Unit 2","title":"Unit 2","sub":"We/They are · familia · adjetivos","rules":"\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>1. TO BE en plural</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">we / you / they</span><span class=\"ra\">are</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">he / she / it</span><span class=\"ra\">is</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">We <b>are</b> tall. They <b>are</b> young. He <b>is</b> my brother.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>2. El negativo: isn't / aren't</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">he / she / it</span><span class=\"ra\">isn't</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">we / you / they</span><span class=\"ra\">aren't</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">We <b>aren't</b> old. He <b>isn't</b> seven.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>3. Respuestas cortas (plural)</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Are they happy?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, they are. / No, they aren't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Is he your brother?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, he is. / No, he isn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>&#9888; Regla de oro:</b> se contesta con <b>el mismo verbo</b> de la pregunta. Si preguntan con <b>Is</b>, contest&aacute;s con <b>is</b>. Si preguntan con <b>Are</b>, contest&aacute;s con <b>are</b>.</div></div>\n","ex":[{"t":"choice","q":"We ___ tall.","o":["am","is","are"],"a":2},{"t":"choice","q":"They ___ young.","o":["is","are","am"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Are they happy?</span>","h":"Respondé que SÍ","o":["Yes, they are.","Yes, they aren't.","Yes, they is."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Is he your brother?</span>","h":"Respondé que NO","o":["No, he aren't.","No, he not.","No, he isn't."],"a":2},{"t":"choice","q":"We ___ old. (negativo)","o":["aren't","isn't","not"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Is she your sister?</span>","h":"Respondé que SÍ","o":["Yes, she is.","Yes, she are.","Yes, he is."],"a":0},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","pairs":[["mum","mamá"],["dad","papá"],["sister","hermana"],["grandma","abuela"],["grandpa","abuelo"],["brother","hermano"],["dog","perro"],["family","familia"]]},{"t":"choice","q":"Lo contrario de <span class='en'>tall</span> es:","o":["small","short","young"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"Lo contrario de <span class='en'>happy</span> es:","o":["sad","old","tall"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"Lo contrario de <span class='en'>young</span> es:","o":["short","small","old"],"a":2},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>hermana</b>","a":"sister"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>abuelo</b>","a":"grandpa"},{"t":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice <b>hermanito bebé</b>?","o":["baby brother","baby sister","little brother"],"a":0}]},{"id":"u3","dot":"🏠","name":"Unit 3","title":"Unit 3","sub":"There is / There are · preposiciones · la casa","rules":"\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>1. There is / There are = \"hay\"</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">1 sola cosa</span><span class=\"ra\">There is</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">2 o m&aacute;s cosas</span><span class=\"ra\">There are</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">There <b>is</b> a tree house. There <b>are</b> four rooms.</p>\n<div class=\"warn\"><span class=\"no\">There is four chairs</span> &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; <span class=\"yes\">There are four chairs</span>. Si el sustantivo termina en <b>-s</b>, va <b>are</b>.</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>2. Preguntas y respuestas</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Is there a ladder?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Are there any stairs?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, there are. / No, there aren't.</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">Igual que antes: el verbo se adelanta y en la respuesta se repite <b>there</b>.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>3. How many...? (cu&aacute;ntos)</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">How many chairs are there?</span><span class=\"ra\">There are six.</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">Despu&eacute;s de <b>How many</b> el sustantivo va siempre en plural (chair<b>s</b>, room<b>s</b>) y se contesta con <b>There are</b> + el n&uacute;mero.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>4. Preposiciones: d&oacute;nde est&aacute; la cosa</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">adentro</span><span class=\"ra\">in</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">encima / sobre</span><span class=\"ra\">on</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">debajo</span><span class=\"ra\">under</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">detr&aacute;s</span><span class=\"ra\">behind</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">adelante de</span><span class=\"ra\">in front of</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">al lado de</span><span class=\"ra\">next to</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">entre (dos cosas)</span><span class=\"ra\">between</span></div></div>\n","ex":[{"t":"choice","q":"There ___ a sofa in the living room.","o":["is","are"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"There ___ four rooms.","o":["is","are"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"There ___ two chairs.","o":["is","are"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Is there a ladder?</span>","h":"Respondé que SÍ","o":["Yes, there is.","Yes, there are.","Yes, it is."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Are there any stairs?</span>","h":"Respondé que NO","o":["No, there isn't.","No, there aren't.","No, they aren't."],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>How many chairs are there?</span>","h":"Hay 6","o":["There is six.","There are six.","They are six."],"a":1},{"t":"choice","e":"🐱📦","q":"El gato está <b>ADENTRO</b> de la caja.","o":["The cat is in the box.","The cat is on the box.","The cat is under the box."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"El perro está <b>DEBAJO</b> de la mesa.","o":["behind the table","under the table","next to the table"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"La pelota está <b>ENTRE</b> las dos sillas.","o":["in front of the chairs","behind the chairs","between the chairs"],"a":2},{"t":"choice","q":"La lámpara está <b>AL LADO</b> de la cama.","o":["next to the bed","under the bed","on the bed"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"El cuadro está <b>DETRÁS</b> del sofá.","o":["in front of the sofa","behind the sofa","on the sofa"],"a":1},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada habitación con su nombre","pairs":[["kitchen","cocina"],["bathroom","baño"],["bedroom","dormitorio"],["dining room","comedor"],["living room","living"]]},{"t":"choice","q":"¿En qué habitación cocinás?","o":["in the bathroom","in the kitchen","in the hall"],"a":1},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>sillón</b>","a":"armchair"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>reloj</b>","a":"clock"},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada mueble con su nombre","pairs":[["table","mesa"],["phone","teléfono"],["picture","cuadro"],["radio","la radio"],["television","televisión"],["sofa","sofá"]]},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Where is the phone?</span>","h":"Está ARRIBA de la mesa","o":["It's on the table.","It's in the table.","It's under the table."],"a":0}]},{"id":"u4","dot":"🧸","name":"Unit 4","title":"Unit 4","sub":"I like / He likes · juguetes · el dormitorio","rules":"\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>1. LIKE: la S de he / she / it</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">I / you / we / they</span><span class=\"ra\">like</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">he / she / it</span><span class=\"ra\">like<b>s</b></span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">I <b>like</b> dolls. He <b>likes</b> robots. She <b>likes</b> monsters.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>2. El negativo: DON'T o DOESN'T</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">I / you / we / they</span><span class=\"ra\">don't like</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">he / she / it</span><span class=\"ra\">doesn't like</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">I <b>don't like</b> trains. She <b>doesn't like</b> trucks.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>3. La pregunta: DO o DOES</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Do you like monsters?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, I do. / No, I don't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Does she like teddy bears?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't.</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\"><b>Do</b> va con I / you / we / they. &nbsp; <b>Does</b> va con he / she / it.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>4. &#11088; La regla m&aacute;s importante de la unidad</h4>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>La S aparece UNA sola vez.</b> Si la S ya est&aacute; en <b>does</b> o <b>doesn't</b>, el verbo va limpio, sin S.<br><br>\n<span class=\"yes\">&#10003;</span> She <b>likes</b> dolls.<br>\n<span class=\"yes\">&#10003;</span> She <b>doesn't like</b> dolls. &nbsp;<span class=\"no\">&#10007;</span> She doesn't <span class=\"no\">likes</span> dolls.<br>\n<span class=\"yes\">&#10003;</span> <b>Does</b> she <b>like</b> dolls? &nbsp;<span class=\"no\">&#10007;</span> Does she <span class=\"no\">likes</span> dolls?<br><br>\n<b>Truco para ella:</b> \"<b>does</b> le roba la S al verbo\".</div></div>\n","ex":[{"t":"choice","q":"I ___ dolls. 😍","o":["like","likes"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"He ___ robots. 😍","o":["like","likes"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"She ___ like trucks. 🙅","o":["don't","doesn't"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"I ___ like trains. 🙅","o":["don't","doesn't"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Do you like monsters?</span>","h":"Respondé que SÍ","o":["Yes, I do.","Yes, I like.","Yes, I does."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Does she like teddy bears?</span>","h":"Respondé que NO","o":["No, she don't.","No, she doesn't.","No, she isn't."],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"___ he like cars?","o":["Do","Does"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"___ you like dolls?","o":["Do","Does"],"a":0},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada juguete con su significado","pairs":[["ball","pelota"],["doll","muñeca"],["teddy bear","osito"],["truck","camión"],["bike","bicicleta"],["boat","barco"]]},{"t":"choice","e":"🛏️","q":"¿Dónde dormís?","o":["in the bed","on the desk","on the rug"],"a":0},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>ventana</b>","a":"window"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>espejo</b>","a":"mirror"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>lámpara</b>","a":"lamp"},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada cosa del dormitorio","pairs":[["bookcase","biblioteca"],["door","puerta"],["wall","pared"],["desk","escritorio"],["rug","alfombra"],["bed","cama"]]}]},{"id":"u5","dot":"🐴","name":"Unit 5","title":"Unit 5","sub":"Can · animales de granja · comida","rules":"\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>1. CAN = poder / saber hacer algo</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">I / you / he / she / we / they</span><span class=\"ra\">can</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\"><b>Can</b> es igual para todos. Nunca lleva S: se dice He <b>can</b> swim, nunca <span class=\"no\">he cans</span>.</p>\n<p class=\"exline\">El verbo que viene despu&eacute;s va solo, sin \"to\": can <b>fly</b>, can <b>swim</b>.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>2. Negativo y preguntas con CAN</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">negativo</span><span class=\"ra\">can't</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Can you swim?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, I can. / No, I can't.</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">They <b>can</b> fly. They <b>can't</b> swim.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>3. Hechos (lo que los animales hacen siempre)</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">horses / they / we (plural)</span><span class=\"ra\">eat</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">a horse / he / she / it</span><span class=\"ra\">eat<b>s</b></span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">Horses <b>eat</b> grass. A cow <b>eats</b> grass. Es la misma S de la Unit 4.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>4. Preguntar por hechos: DO / DOES</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Do they eat carrots?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, they do. / No, they don't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Does it eat meat?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, it does. / No, it doesn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>&#9888; No mezclar:</b> si la pregunta empieza con <b>Can</b>, se contesta <b>can</b>. Si empieza con <b>Do</b>, se contesta <b>do</b>.<br>\nCan you swim? &rarr; <span class=\"yes\">Yes, I can</span>, no <span class=\"no\">Yes, I do</span>.</div></div>\n","ex":[{"t":"choice","e":"🐦","q":"Birds ___ fly.","o":["can","can't"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","e":"🐴","q":"Horses ___ fly.","o":["can","can't"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Can you swim?</span>","h":"Respondé que SÍ","o":["Yes, I can.","Yes, I do.","Yes, I am."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Can you fly?</span>","h":"Respondé que NO","o":["No, I don't.","No, I can't.","No, I am not."],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"Horses ___ grass.","o":["eat","eats"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Do they eat meat?</span>","h":"Los caballos NO comen carne","o":["No, they don't.","No, they aren't.","No, they can't."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Do we eat carrots?</span>","h":"Respondé que SÍ","o":["Yes, we can.","Yes, we do.","Yes, we are."],"a":1},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada animal con su nombre","pairs":[["cow","vaca"],["duck","pato"],["sheep","oveja"],["goat","cabra"],["donkey","burro"],["chicken","gallina"]]},{"t":"choice","e":"🍉","q":"<span class='en'>What is it?</span>","o":["It's a watermelon.","It's a lettuce.","It's corn."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","e":"🐰🥕","q":"Rabbits eat ___.","o":["meat","bread","carrots"],"a":2},{"t":"choice","q":"El elefante es muy ___.","o":["strong","tired","smart"],"a":0},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>maíz</b>","a":"corn"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>pan</b>","a":"bread"},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada comida con su nombre","pairs":[["apples","manzanas"],["tomatoes","tomates"],["bread","pan"],["lettuce","lechuga"],["watermelons","sandías"],["corn","maíz"]]},{"t":"choice","e":"🍌","q":"<span class='en'>What is it?</span>","o":["It's a banana.","It's an apple.","It's corn."],"a":0}]},{"id":"u6","dot":"🐞","name":"Unit 6","title":"Unit 6","sub":"Have got · this/that/these/those · el cuerpo","rules":"\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>1. HAVE GOT = tener (van siempre juntas)</h4>\n<p class=\"exline\"><b>have got</b> es una sola expresi&oacute;n que significa \"tener\". No se separan ni se traducen por partes.</p>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">I / you / we / they</span><span class=\"ra\">have got</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">he / she / it</span><span class=\"ra\">has got</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">I <b>have got</b> a dog. &nbsp; She <b>has got</b> a cat. &nbsp; A snake <b>has got</b> no legs.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>2. &#11088; Lo que cambia es HAVE / HAS. \"GOT\" nunca cambia</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">yo, vos, nosotros, ellos</span><span class=\"ra\">HAVE + got</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">&eacute;l, ella, un animal, una cosa</span><span class=\"ra\">HAS + got</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\">Nunca existe <span class=\"no\">\"hases\"</span>, <span class=\"no\">\"gots\"</span> ni <span class=\"no\">\"haves\"</span>. La palabra <b>got</b> se escribe siempre igual, en todas las frases.</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>3. Negativo y pregunta</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">I / you / we / they</span><span class=\"ra\">haven't got</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">he / she / it</span><span class=\"ra\">hasn't got</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Have you got a dog?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Has it got any legs?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, it has. / No, it hasn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>&#9888; Error t&iacute;pico:</b> en la respuesta corta <b>NO se repite \"got\"</b>.<br>\n<span class=\"yes\">&#10003;</span> Yes, I <b>have</b>. &nbsp;&nbsp; <span class=\"no\">&#10007;</span> Yes, I have <span class=\"no\">got</span>.</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>4. This / That / These / Those</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">cerca &mdash; 1 cosa</span><span class=\"ra\">this</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">cerca &mdash; varias</span><span class=\"ra\">these</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">lejos &mdash; 1 cosa</span><span class=\"ra\">that</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">lejos &mdash; varias</span><span class=\"ra\">those</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\"><b>This</b> is a mouse. &nbsp; <b>These</b> are bees. &nbsp; <b>That</b> is a snake. &nbsp; <b>Those</b> are butterflies.</p>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>Truco:</b> <b>these</b> y <b>those</b> terminan en <b>-se</b> &rarr; son los <b>plurales</b>. Y si la palabra es plural, el verbo tambi&eacute;n: <b>These are</b>, <b>Those are</b>.</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>5. Preguntar qu&eacute; es</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">1 cosa</span><span class=\"ra\">What is this / that?</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">varias</span><span class=\"ra\">What are these / those?</span></div></div>\n","ex":[{"t":"choice","q":"I ___ got a dog.","o":["have","has"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"A snake ___ got any legs. 🐍","o":["haven't","hasn't"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Have you got any lizards?</span>","h":"Respondé que SÍ","o":["Yes, I have.","Yes, I has.","Yes, I am."],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"<span class='en'>Has it got any legs?</span>","h":"Respondé que NO","o":["No, it haven't.","No, it hasn't.","No, it isn't."],"a":1},{"t":"choice","q":"___ this a spider?","o":["Is","Are"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"___ these butterflies?","o":["Is","Are"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","e":"🐝🐝","q":"Cerca y en plural: ___ are bees.","o":["This","These","That"],"a":1},{"t":"choice","e":"🦋🦋","q":"Lejos y en plural: ___ are butterflies.","o":["These","That","Those"],"a":2},{"t":"choice","e":"🐭","q":"Cerca y singular: ___ is a mouse.","o":["This","These","Those"],"a":0},{"t":"choice","q":"¿Cómo preguntás por varias cosas?","o":["What is these?","What are these?","What are this?"],"a":1},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada bichito con su nombre","pairs":[["bee","abeja"],["frog","rana"],["spider","araña"],["butterfly","mariposa"],["ladybug","vaquita de San Antonio"],["caterpillar","oruga"]]},{"t":"match","q":"Uní cada parte del cuerpo","pairs":[["head","cabeza"],["hand","mano"],["leg","pierna"],["mouth","boca"],["ear","oreja"],["nose","nariz"]]},{"t":"choice","q":"El plural de <span class='en'>foot</span> es:","o":["foots","feet","footes"],"a":1},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>ojo</b>","a":"eye"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>pelo</b>","a":"hair"},{"t":"spell","q":"Escribí en inglés: <b>brazo</b>","a":"arm"}]},{"id":"resumen","dot":"U0001F4CB","name":"Resumen","title":"Resumen general","sub":"¿Cuándo uso cada uno? — la chuleta final","rules":"\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>1. Primero: &iquest;qu&eacute; quer&eacute;s decir?</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">ser, estar, edad, c&oacute;mo es algo</span><span class=\"ra\">am / is / are</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">tener algo</span><span class=\"ra\">have got / has got</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">gustar, comer, acciones y hechos</span><span class=\"ra\">do / does</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">poder o saber hacer algo</span><span class=\"ra\">can</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">hay (cosas en un lugar)</span><span class=\"ra\">there is / there are</span></div>\n<p class=\"exline\">Esta es la decisi&oacute;n m&aacute;s importante. Todo lo dem&aacute;s sale de ac&aacute;.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>2. Despu&eacute;s: &iquest;qui&eacute;n hace la acci&oacute;n?</h4>\n<p class=\"exline\">Hay <b>dos grupos</b> y es lo &uacute;nico que hay que memorizar:</p>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\"><b>Grupo A</b> &mdash; I, you, we, they</span><span class=\"ra\">are &middot; have got &middot; like &middot; do / don't</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\"><b>Grupo B</b> &mdash; he, she, it</span><span class=\"ra\">is &middot; has got &middot; likes &middot; does / doesn't</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>El Grupo B es el de la S:</b> i<b>s</b>, ha<b>s</b>, like<b>s</b>, doe<b>s</b>. Si el sujeto es <b>&eacute;l, ella, un animal o una cosa</b>, casi todo lleva S.<br>\n(<b>I</b> es la excepci&oacute;n: va con <b>am</b>.)</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>3. Respuestas cortas: se contesta con el MISMO verbo</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Are you...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, I am. / No, I'm not.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Is he...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, he is. / No, he isn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Do you like...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, I do. / No, I don't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Does she like...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Have you got...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Has it got...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, it has. / No, it hasn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Can you...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, I can. / No, I can't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Is there...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Are there...?</span><span class=\"ra\">Yes, there are. / No, there aren't.</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>&#9888; El error m&aacute;s com&uacute;n de toda la prueba:</b> contestar con el verbo equivocado.<br>\nDo you like dolls? &rarr; <span class=\"no\">&#10007; Yes, I am.</span> &nbsp; <span class=\"yes\">&#10003; Yes, I do.</span><br>\nMir&aacute; con qu&eacute; palabra <b>empieza</b> la pregunta y contest&aacute; con esa misma.</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"rsec\"><h4>4. Las tres S que confunden</h4>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">He like<b>s</b> dolls.</span><span class=\"ra\">afirmativo &rarr; S en el verbo</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">He doe<b>s</b>n't like dolls.</span><span class=\"ra\">negativo &rarr; S en doesn't</span></div>\n<div class=\"rrow\"><span class=\"rl\">Doe<b>s</b> he like dolls?</span><span class=\"ra\">pregunta &rarr; S en does</span></div>\n<div class=\"warn\"><b>La S va en un solo lugar por frase.</b> Si ya la us&oacute; <b>does</b> o <b>doesn't</b>, el verbo queda sin S.</div></div>\n","ex":[]}]